    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-279425",
      "knowledge_point_id": "bea036e3-19cd-572b-a6cb-2fa466c2a399",
      "knowledge_point": "Interpreting a Given Matrix as a Rotation",
      "problem": "What is the geometrical interpretation of the transformation represented by the matrix $A$ given below? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A$ given above represents a rotation of \n{{field-1}}\nradians clockwise about the origin.",
      "worked_solution": "The rotation matrix ${R}_{\\theta }$ represents a rotation of angle $\\theta $ counterclockwise about the origin and is given by\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nComparing $A$ with the rotation matrix, we have \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta >0$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta <0$ we must have that $\\theta $ lies in $4$th quadrant. \n\nDividing the first equation by the second gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}=-\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nThe principal value $\\theta $ is\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ radians *clockwise* about the origin.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{\\pi}{3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{\\pi}{6}"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "\\frac{\\pi}{3}",
          "choices_complete": false,
          "correct_origin": "model_interpretation"
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-279425",
