    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-170529",
      "knowledge_point_id": "bea036e3-19cd-572b-a6cb-2fa466c2a399",
      "knowledge_point": "Interpreting a Given Matrix as a Rotation",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055662/assets/31511ef5aa3ae263673703dcc2f66f14fdcaf1d367c4ef680e075bbece1a561c.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The rotation matrix ${R}_{\\theta }$ represents a rotation of angle $\\theta $ counterclockwise about the origin and is given by\n\n$$\n{R}_{\\theta }=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComparing $A$ with the rotation matrix, we have \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta >0$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta <0,$  we must have that $\\theta $ lies in $2$nd quadrant. \n\nDividing the first equation by the second gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-1.\n$$\n\nThe principal value of ${\\theta }_{1}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\theta }_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\n$$\n\nbut this is outside the range $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le x\\le \\pi .$ To find a value in the required range, we add $\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\theta ={\\theta }_{1}+\\pi =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our matrix represents a rotation of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin.\n\nFinally, to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055662/assets/49ec5421325f8ae5492743b988b1c0d727b2eac9e56f169ad5d55753bae5d69a.png)",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
