    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-11965",
      "knowledge_point_id": "b2371a64-5e91-5caa-91c0-f6c7ff572c70",
      "knowledge_point": "Rotating an Object About the Origin",
      "problem": "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,-2),(0,4),(2,-2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under a counterclockwise rotation of ${45}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(0,-2\\sqrt{2})$\n- $(1,-\\sqrt{3})$\n- $(2\\sqrt{2},0)$",
      "worked_solution": "The rotation matrix ${R}_{\\theta }$ represents a rotation of angle $\\theta $ counterclockwise about the origin and is given by\n\n$$\n{R}_{\\theta }=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\theta ={45}^{∘}$ into the above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({45}^{∘}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the transformation, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the rotation $R$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\sqrt{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are \n\n$$\n(0,-2\\sqrt{2}),\\,(-2\\sqrt{2},2\\sqrt{2}),\\,(2\\sqrt{2},0).\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "answer_fields": [
